    "result_text": "The full suite is green (11 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field so that a created owner returns its name formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nTwo changes, following the app's existing OpenAPI-driven, MapStruct-based conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `readOnly` `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. Because the app generates its DTOs from this spec, this adds `getDisplayName()`/`setDisplayName()` to the generated `OwnerDto` and exposes it in the API response. Being `readOnly`, it stays out of the input (`OwnerFields`) so it can't be supplied on create.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes `displayName` as `lastName + \", \" + firstName` from the stored names, so both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses carry the formatted value.\n\nThe new `Cp05Tests.coreComputesDisplayName` passes, and all 11 tests remain green.",
